          "settings": {
            "text": "Surrey Arts and Craft Home",
            "heading_tag": "h1"
          }
        },
        "richtext_BiJLfL": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>This Arts and Crafts country house is a bucolic period property that, over the course of two years, was sensitively and comprehensively restored and renovated. In need of significant attention, the house was carefully reconfigured to support the needs of a modern, dynamic family, while a deep respect for the original architecture guided every decision.<br/><br/>Studio Peake led the creative direction across the entire project, shaping the aesthetic of each space in close collaboration with a team of architects, lighting designers, and specialist contractors. Antiques were sourced throughout to anchor the interiors in their setting, while layered textiles, colour, and texture were used to create rooms that feel warm, characterful, and deeply personal.<br/><br/>The result is a welcoming family home that honours its Arts and Crafts heritage while embracing comfort, individuality, and contemporary living.</p>"
          }
        },
